<title>ABU DHABI: TABLE-UAE's Union National Bank 1996 H2 results.</title>
<headline>TABLE-UAE's Union National Bank 1996 H2 results.</headline>
<dateline>ABU DHABI 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to December 31, 1996 vs five years and six months to June 30, 1996.</p>
<p>(million dirhams unless stated)</p>
<p> Net profit		   37.174	  vs   74.716</p>
<p> Earnings per share	  9.60 dirhams vs   19.29 dirhams</p>
<p> Net interest income	80.733	  vs  646.377</p>
<p> Net operating income    125.216	  vs  938.329</p>
<p> Provisions		   25.000	  vs  289.872</p>
<p>Retained earnings:</p>
<p> - at beginning of period 60.154	  vs    0.382</p>
<p> - at end of period	 59.894	  vs   60.154</p>
<p> Assets			  5.65 bln     vs    5.48 bln</p>
<p> Loans and advances	  3.28 bln     vs    3.73 bln</p>
<p> Customers' deposits	 4.98 bln     vs    4.84 bln</p>
<p>Full name: Union National Bank, formerly Bank of Credit and Commerce (Emirates).</p>
<p>NOTE: In December 1996 Union National Bank submitted its first results to shareholders for approval since the collapse in July 1991 of majority shareholder Bank of Credit and Commerce International (BCCI). -- Dubai newsroom +9714 6071 222</p>
</text>
